<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/normal_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: question on trios &nbsp;(Read 213 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=869" title="View the profile of Remedie">Remedie</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 5<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.kompewtaz.com/eq/catav.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=869"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11512#msg11512"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11512#msg11512">question on trios</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> September 30, 2004, 05:47:18 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Hi guys<br /><br /><br />ok perhaps not a thread strictly about class discussion but I&#039;m not sure where to ask this.<br /><br /><br />I need advice on three classes that would work well together in the low-mid level game.<br /><br />so far we&#039;ve tried beastlord/mage/necro and paladin/shaman/ranger<br /><br />anyone got any other ideas that we may not have thought of?<br /><br /><br />Thanks!
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><img src="http://www.kompewtaz.com/eq/remsig.jpg" alt="" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11515"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202" title="View the profile of xaanru">xaanru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 51<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								I&#039;m not a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.sonsofkings.com" title="Sons of Kings Guild" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11515#msg11515"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11515#msg11515">Re: question on trios</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> September 30, 2004, 06:44:41 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well, best seems to be a combo of 1) some healer type, 2) tank/hybrid and 3) caster/dps of some sort.<br /><br />Cleric/SK/enchanter works even at level 67, although many permutations are possible.<br /><br />If you like dungeons, perhaps a druid for healer, or a wizard for caster (think evac and port here). Of course, if you have a wizard, maybe you&#039;d prefer a shaman for healer, as you&#039;d be without a slower otherwise.<br /><br />Outside, maybe ranger for dps, because they are good pullers with harmony, shaman for heal/slow and Pally for tank, to help with the heals.<br /><br />Honestly, the possibilities are endless. Depends how creatively you play.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Xaanru 66th lvl Archon of Marr <br />&lt;Sons of Kings&gt; Rodcet Nife <br />Grandmaster Smith(250)* GM Trophy<br />Grandmaster Jeweler (250)<br />Grandmaster Tailor (250)<br />Master Baker(200)<br />Master Fletcher (200)<br />Master Jeweler (200)<br />Master Brewer (200)<br />Master Potter (194)<br />Master Fisherman (186)<br />Master Drunk (189)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11526"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52" title="View the profile of Gabus">Gabus</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 276<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/psychotic-day.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I beat the Internet. The end guy was hard.<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11526#msg11526"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11526#msg11526">Re: question on trios</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> October 01, 2004, 10:53:34 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Is this trio supposed to be 3 boxed? If so, then the equasion changes a little, as you want 2 of the boxes to be effective with macros. Also for those posting remember he said &quot;Mid level game.&quot; That leaves some room for interpretation. Many classes (paladin) dont really come into their own untill high 50&#039;s. I am assuming that 45 - 60 is what you mean by mid level.<br /><br />I think you have to think of the basic &quot;Holy Trinity&quot; ideas when you work on this idea. Who covers the trinity, and what &quot;extras&quot; do they bring to the table. In my mind, you need healing, slowing, and tanking, at a minimum. The trio should start there.<br /><br />Off the top of my head, I think the following trio would be good.<br /><br />1) Druid - Heals/buffs, Extras: ease of travel, (still can be handy to have someone to SoW, and port. Even in the age of stones) and some nice DPS. Snare, Harmony outside.<br /><br />2) Paladin - Tanks. Extras: Paladin heals in the midrange are good for downtime. Snap aggro without much maintenence. Res is available for those awkward moments. Paci works up to 55.<br /><br />3) Shaman - Slows. Extras: Great buffs for the Tank, best slows, buffs, and even debuffs, with some solid DPS (dots), and healing. SoW.<br /><br />Druid and Shaman are easily botted and macro&#039;d. Paladin DPS is laughable in the midrange, but should be able to make solid use of the dots the Shaman, and Druid can bring to the table, significantly shortening the fight. (Read: the dots will go full duration) I have boxed my paladin with a shaman, and a druid, and I often wished I had been able to 3 box that combo.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=139779" target="_blank">Gabus Magelo Profile</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11534"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=869" title="View the profile of Remedie">Remedie</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 5<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.kompewtaz.com/eq/catav.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=869"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11534#msg11534"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1162.msg11534#msg11534">Re: question on trios</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> October 01, 2004, 06:26:34 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							thanks Gabus!<br /><br /><br />(firstly it&#039;s she not he lol)<br /><br /><br />this is not for a 3 box idea though it&#039;s three separate players starting from scratch on a different server heh and because of the complete lack of twinkage options it&#039;s likely that it&#039;ll be a slow road (intentionally) which is why I said low-mid level.<br /><br />I&#039;ve heard people talk about the &#039;holy trinity&#039; often and wondered if that was three classes or three abilities so thanks for clearing that up .. we were also thinking pulling snaring buffing and rezzing needed to be put with that.<br /><br />As far as the suggestions, none of us are prepared to make a druid or an sk (no offense), one is inclined to try a monk, so perhaps a monk, pally, shaman or if we can talk him out of it a pally, shm, ranger will be it I&#039;m not sure.<br /><br /><br /><br />But thanks for your suggestions .. it&#039;s reassuring to know we&#039;re sorta on the right track at least lol<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
